WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.579
Two readers, one report.

2
00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:04.077
Your report has at least two audiences.

3
00:00:04.357 --> 00:00:14.256
One is a decision-maker (a hiring manager, a client lead, a head of delivery) who wants to know what the system does, how well, at what cost, and whether to use it.

4
00:00:14.536 --> 00:00:20.360
The other is an engineer who wants to know whether to believe you, and could reproduce your numbers if you let them.

5
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:32.267
Google’s Technical Writing One course suggests defining your audience by role first and then by proximity: how close each reader is to the specific knowledge, and how recently they used it.

6
00:00:32.547 --> 00:00:39.331
A staff engineer who has never built a RAG system and a PM who has used one daily are close in different ways.

7
00:00:39.611 --> 00:00:44.432
The same unit names the trap you are most likely to fall into: the curse of knowledge.

8
00:00:44.712 --> 00:00:51.923
After six weeks inside your project, “TNR,” “should-abstain,” and “the held-out split” feel like ordinary words.

9
00:00:52.203 --> 00:00:54.229
To your decision-maker they are noise.

10
00:00:54.509 --> 00:00:57.539
The fix is structural, not a matter of dumbing down.

11
00:00:57.819 --> 00:01:07.205
The course’s documents unit recommends stating scope and audience at the start and putting the key points up front, because readers may stop after the first paragraph.

12
00:01:07.485 --> 00:01:20.989
So the report template opens with a one-paragraph summary written for the decision-maker, in plain words: the user, the job, how well it works compared with the baseline, what it costs, the biggest risk, and the recommendation.

13
00:01:21.269 --> 00:01:28.011
Everything an engineer needs goes in the sections and appendices that follow, where precision matters more than brevity.

14
00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:31.704
Test the summary on a real person outside engineering.

15
00:01:31.984 --> 00:01:37.296
Ask them to tell you, in their own words, what the system does, how well, and what the main risk is.

16
00:01:37.576 --> 00:01:40.200
If they can’t, rewrite the summary, not the reader.
